BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 453.5 Td (2016 to May 2026. The model identifies three latent market states - bull, sideways, and bear - by) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 440.0 Td (learning the characteristic return and volatility of each state from the data rather than applying) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 426.5 Td (manual labels.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 408.0 Td (The model converged cleanly. The three states separate primarily on volatility rather than return) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 394.5 Td (direction. The bear state has a mean monthly return of 0.002 and a standard deviation of 0.075 -) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 381.0 Td (nearly identical in return to the sideways state but dramatically more volatile. This is economically) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 367.5 Td (sensible: the defining feature of a crisis regime is not that returns are negative but that uncertainty) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 354.0 Td (is extreme. March and April 2020 are correctly labelled bear; June 2021 bull; June 2022 bear.) Tj ET
